description:
Sends a short report about Neumann to the team that builds it. They read every report and use it to fix problems and decide what to build, so honest feedback, good or bad, is useful. Use this when:
- a Neumann tool returned an error (send it right away), behaved unexpectedly or gave a result that looks wrong;
- the user needs something no Neumann tool can do, or an option that is missing;
- a description, output or error message was confusing;
- a session in which you used Neumann is ending: send one short report even if everything worked. Knowing which tools did the job for which kind of task is useful data, not noise.
Do not send one after a routine successful call mid-session. Put several points in one report: a signed-in account may send 5 per hour and 20 per day, and callers without an account share 60 per hour and 300 per day. Only message is required. Fill in the other fields that apply so the team can act without guessing. Write in your own words. Never include personal data (names, email addresses, company names), the user's own numbers (inputs or results), secrets or keys, or the conversation transcript; describe the task and any wrong result in general terms instead. Tell the user you are sending it. Add sender_email only if the user wants a reply. If you are signed in, your account id is included. No account is needed. It returns status "sent". Cost: free, with or without an account -- it debits no credits and spends none of your free daily runs.
